.SS "double csmp::EOS_CO2H2ONaCl_Spycher04::activityCoefficientDuanSun2003 (double temperature, double pressure, double mSalt)"
Computes the solubility of CO2 in brine

.PP
\fBDuan\fP and Sun 2003

.PP
An improved model calculating CO2 solubility in pure water and aqueous NaCl solutions from 257 to 533 K and from 0 to 2000 bar Chem\&. Geol\&. 193, 257-272

.PP
we can find it also in Spycher et al (2004), CO2-H2O Mixtures in the Geological Sequestration of CO2\&. II\&. Partitioning in Chloride Brines at 12-100oC and up to 600 bar

.PP
T in C P in Pa (total pressure: PCo2 + PH2o) mSalt molality in mol/Kg activityCoefficient without unit

.PP
range T: from 273 to 533 K range P: from 0 to 2000 bar ionic strength: from 0 to 4\&.3 m up to 6m NaCl molality up to 4m CaCl molality

.PP
This version is just valid for NaCl [mNaCl](mK=mCa=mMg=mSo4=0) 
